cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Dynamic dimensional reduction in the Abelian sandpile: a Lean 4 formalization"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Dynamic dimensional
  reduction in the Abelian sandpile" (Bou-Rabee), in a corrected edition of its arXiv
  source: dimensional reduction and self-similarity of the parallel toppling odometer,
  the corollary for the sandpile, and the regularity proposition proved with them by one
  joint induction over dimension, side length and time. All 23 theorem-level statements of the corrected edition (its versions of the 20 statement clauses of the published paper, and three added lemmas) are proved in Lean, with no `sorry` and only the standard axioms. Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 1.1 are stated as published, with the quantifier in the definition of `τ_j` made explicit.
  Each of the four Mathlib-only comparator challenges contains intentional
  statement-level sorrys, whose solutions are checked separately.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Abelian sandpile
  - parallel toppling
  - dimensional reduction
license: Apache-2.0
